@startuml Sequence_3
hide footbox
title Scenario 3: Enemy Turn — Goblin Attack Reduced by Warrior's DefendBuff

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor       "User"                         as User
boundary    "ArenaBattleScreen"            as Screen
control     "GameApp\n<<ActionCallbacks>>" as App
control     "BattleEngine"                 as Engine
entity      "Goblin\n<<Enemy>>"            as Goblin
control     "BasicEnemyActionStrategy"     as Strategy
entity      "Warrior\n<<Player>>"          as Warrior
entity      "DefendBuff\n<<StatusEffect>>" as Buff
entity      "GameState\n<<Static>>"        as State

note over User, State
  This is the enemy phase of the same executePlayerTurn() call as Scenario 2.
  Warrior (SPD=30) already defended — DefendBuff is active (turns=2, defenseBoost=+10).
  Now: Goblin (SPD=25) acts and hits a hardened Warrior.
end note

' ── User Input (same round as Scenario 2) ──────────────────────
User -> Screen : clicks "Defend" button
note right of User
  Same user action that triggered Scenario 2.
  Shown here for continuity — this enemy phase
  happens in the same executePlayerTurn() call.
end note

Screen -> App : callbacks.onDefend()
App -> Engine : executePlayerTurn(choice=2, target=0, null)
note right of App : choice=2 → Defend branch

note over Engine
  Warrior phase: defend() ran, DefendBuff applied.
  (See Scenario 2 for player phase detail.)
  Now processing: Goblin (instanceof Enemy).
end note

' ── Goblin Phase ───────────────────────────────────────────────
Engine -> Goblin : beginTurn()
note over Goblin
  No active effects.
  canAct = true → returns true.
end note
Goblin --> Engine : true

Engine -> Goblin : getStrategy()
Goblin --> Engine : BasicEnemyActionStrategy

Engine -> Strategy : execute(goblin, [warrior])
Strategy -> Warrior : isAlive()
Warrior --> Strategy : true

Strategy -> Goblin : getAttack()
Goblin --> Strategy : 35

Strategy -> Warrior : getDefense()
note over Warrior
  Iterates activeEffects → finds DefendBuff.
  calls DefendBuff.modifyDefense(baseDefense=20)
end note
Warrior -> Buff : modifyDefense(20)
note over Buff : returns 20 + defenseBoost(10) = 30
Buff --> Warrior : 30
Warrior --> Strategy : 30

note over Strategy
  damage = max(0, 35 − 30) = 5
  Reduced from 15 (Scenario 1) to 5
  because DefendBuff boosted Warrior's defense.
end note

Strategy -> Warrior : takeDamage(5, goblin)
note over Warrior
  Iterates activeEffects.
  DefendBuff.modifyIncomingDamage(5,...) = 5 (no override).
  hp -= 5
end note
Warrior --> Strategy : 5 (damage dealt)
Strategy --> Engine : done

Engine -> Engine : lastPlayerDamage = 5
Engine -> Engine : pendingTurnFrames.add(\n  TurnFrame("Goblin attacks.", playerDamage=5))
Engine -> Engine : sweepDeadEnemies()
note over Engine : Goblin hp > 0 — nothing removed.

' ── End of Round ───────────────────────────────────────────────
Engine -> State : checkEndCondition()
State --> Engine : 0 (continue)
Engine -> Engine : endRound()
Engine --> App : 0 (continue)

' ── Render Result ──────────────────────────────────────────────
App -> Engine : drainTurnFrames()
Engine --> App : [TurnFrame("Warrior defends."), TurnFrame("Goblin attacks.", dmg=5)]
App -> Screen : render(ArenaViewState, floatingDamage=5 on Warrior)
Screen --> User : updated battle screen\n(Warrior HP reduced by only 5 — DefendBuff visible)

@enduml
